# Netlify serves these headers with every response (this file is copied verbatim from public/
# into dist/ at build time). Before this file the only security header in production was HSTS,
# which meant the dashboard could be framed by any origin — i.e. clickjacking was possible on a
# money/commission UI.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy here on purpose: it has to be tailored to the Vite bundle and to the
# AWS AppStream + PDF iframes the app embeds, so a guessed policy would break the Kaizen demo and
# the invoice previews. Tracked as a follow-up.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  # microphone=(self) — needed by Sofia's dictation (2026-08-13). An empty list,
  # microphone=(), blocks the API for EVERY origin including this page, so the
  # browser refuses before any of our code runs and the failure is silent.
  # (self) opens it to this origin only; geolocation and camera stay closed.
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(self), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
